 - The interface `IContentItemIndexHandler` was renamed to `IDocumentIndexHandler`.
 - The `IndexingConstants` class was renamed to `ContentIndexingConstants`.
+
+### Content Types Module
+
+#### Content Definition Event Handler Migration
+
+The `IContentDefinitionEventHandler` interface has been marked as obsolete and will be removed in a future version. All content definition events are now consolidated in the `IContentDefinitionHandler` interface to provide a unified approach for handling both content definition building and lifecycle events.
+
+**Key Changes:**
+
+- `IContentDefinitionEventHandler` is now marked as `[Obsolete]`
+- `IContentDefinitionHandler` has been extended with all event methods from `IContentDefinitionEventHandler`
+- Event methods in `IContentDefinitionHandler` have default (empty) implementations, so existing implementations only need to implement the building methods
+- `ContentDefinitionManager` now triggers events instead of `ContentDefinitionService`
+- Backward compatibility is maintained during the transition period
+
+**Migration Path:**
+
+1. **For new implementations**: Implement `IContentDefinitionHandler` instead of `IContentDefinitionEventHandler`
+2. **For existing implementations**: 
+   - Continue using `IContentDefinitionEventHandler` (it will continue to work)
+   - When ready to migrate, implement `IContentDefinitionHandler` and remove `IContentDefinitionEventHandler`
+   - Register your service as `IContentDefinitionHandler` instead of `IContentDefinitionEventHandler`
+
+**Example Migration:**
+
+```csharp
+// Old approach (still works but obsolete)
+public class MyEventHandler : IContentDefinitionEventHandler
+{
+    public void ContentTypeCreated(ContentTypeCreatedContext context) 
+    {
+        // Your logic here
+    }
+    
+    public void ContentTypeUpdated(ContentTypeUpdatedContext context) { }
+    // ... implement all other required methods
+}
+
+// New approach (recommended)
+public class MyEventHandler : IContentDefinitionHandler
+{
+    // Required building methods
+    public void ContentTypeBuilding(ContentTypeBuildingContext context) { }
+    public void ContentPartBuilding(ContentPartBuildingContext context) { }
+    public void ContentTypePartBuilding(ContentTypePartBuildingContext context) { }
+    public void ContentPartFieldBuilding(ContentPartFieldBuildingContext context) { }
+    
+    // Event methods (override only what you need)
+    public void ContentTypeCreated(ContentTypeCreatedContext context) 
+    {
+        // Your logic here
+    }
+    
+    // Other event methods have default implementations, no need to implement them
+}
+
+// Service registration
+services.AddScoped<IContentDefinitionHandler, MyEventHandler>();
+```
+
+This change improves consistency and ensures proper separation of concerns by centralizing all content definition event handling in the `ContentDefinitionManager`.
 - The `BuildIndexContext` class was renamed to `BuildDocumentIndexContext`.
 - In the `BuildDocumentIndexContext` class, the `ContentItem` property was removed. Instead, you should use the new `Record` property. You may check if `Record` in `ContentItem` like this:
 
